orm $(t+p{)}^{2}=q.$ Find $\\,pq\\,,$ and the sum of the roots ${t}_{1}+{t}_{2}.$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399745 1072 #uuid "fac39442-17f5-5ace-9954-931f61698611" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399745 1074 "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-14t+5 & =5 \\\\ {t}^{2}-14t & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-2\\cdot t\\cdot 7+{7}^{2}-{7}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (t-7{)}^{2}-{7}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (t-7{)}^{2} & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=-7$ and $q=49.$ Thus, $pq=-343.$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-7{)}^{2} & =49 \\\\ \\sqrt{(t-7{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ |t-7| & =7 \\\\ t-7 & =\\pm 7 \\\\ t & =7\\pm 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =7-7=0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =7+7=14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum is ${t}_{1}+{t}_{2}=14.$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399746 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399747 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399746 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399748 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399746 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399749 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399746 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399750 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399746 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399751 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399746 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399746 1077 "selection" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399746 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399751 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399746 1080 #uuid "9feed68a-3a5e-5bf8-a32b-19c5c668ac59" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399747 1081 "$pq=-264\\,$ and $\\,{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}=-14$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399747 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399747 1084 #uuid "88f1c5a8-42ee-5523-84ec-f29f28e0ac2c" 13194139533479 17592186045