9 17592186045585 true] [17592186399772 1084 #uuid "ab45afe2-3455-59a3-8889-5adbe62eaacf" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399773 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399774 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399773 1069 "q-112612" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399773 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399773 1071 "The equation $-4{z}^{2}-16z-7=0$ can be written in the form $4(z+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p,$ and solve the equation." 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399773 1072 #uuid "b0945056-0521-55d9-80fa-5db83ff53407" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399773 1074 "First, we multiply the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-4{z}^{2}-16z-7) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 4{z}^{2}+16z+7 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{z}^{2}+16z+7 & =0 \\\\ 4{z}^{2}+16z & =-7 \\\\ 4({z}^{2}+4z) & =-7 \\\\ 4[{z}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot z+{(2)}^{2}-{(2)}^{2}] & =-7 \\\\ 4[{(z+2)}^{2}-4] & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(z+2)}^{2}-4\\cdot 4 & =-7 \\\\ 4{(z+2)}^{2}-16 & =-7 \\\\ 4{(z+2)}^{2} & =-7+16 \\\\ 4{(z+2)}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=2.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(z+2)}^{2} & =9 \\\\ {(z+2)}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(z+2)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}} \\\\ |z+2| & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ z+2 & =\\pm \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ z & =-2\\pm \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-2-\\frac{3}{2}=-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ z & =-2+\\frac{3}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $z=-\\frac{7}{2}$ and $z=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399774 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399775 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399774 1075 #edb/ref 17592