a-15f1f1697f89" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399780 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399781 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399780 1069 "q-112863" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399780 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399780 1071 "According to the rational roots theorem, which of the following could be a root of the polynomial $f(x)=7{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+x-14?$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399780 1072 #uuid "8da2d1e9-08f2-56a5-bfb7-528f2e2d7e75" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399780 1074 "Given a polynomial with integer coefficients, the rational roots theorem states that any rational roots of the polynomial must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial $f(x),$ the constant term is $-14,$ and the leading coefficient is $7.$ So, any rational roots of $f(x)$ must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of }-14}{\\text{factor of }7}.\n$$\n\nOf the given answer choices, only $-2=\\frac{-2}{1}$ takes the above form since the numerator $(-2)$ is a factor of $-14$ and the denominator $(1)$ is a factor of $7.$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399781 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399782 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399781 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399783 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399781 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399784 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399781 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399785 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399781 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399786 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399781 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399781 1077 "selection" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399781 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399786 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399781 1080 #uuid "06a9f0fc-0a9d-5636-9f7e-da5babeb1d8f" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399782 1081 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399782 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399782 1084 #uuid "dec68e86-8f08-510f-8171-dc1ae0f4f3b7" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399783 1081 "3" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399783 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399783 1084 #uuid "1000ee85-77e8-514d-87b6-5fa6ba7c90fc" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399784 1081 "-\\frac{3}{7}" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399784 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399784 1084 #uuid "a5a7fad0-aec1-568c-9216-1773d3768409" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399785 1081 "-4" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399785 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399785 1084 #uuid "62c60f36-b157-50e0-b5d9-80c8be74ad99" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399786 1081 "-2" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399786 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399786 1084 #uuid "1e872297-3c68-5e8b-85d5-47d2da2edc63" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399787 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399788 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399787 1069 "q-113176" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399787 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399787 1071 "Determine the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{8}-4{x}^{4}+2x}{{x}^{6}-1}.$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399787 1072 #uuid "6076d1df-0a51-5be4-8eb1-e4f9aaadd8b8" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399787 1074 "To find the horizontal asymptote of a rational function, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by the dominant term in the denominator, and then we let $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIgnoring the coefficient, the dominant term in the denominator is ${x}^{6}.$ So, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by ${x}^{6},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{8}-4{x}^{4}+2x}{{x}^{6}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{8}}{{x}^{6}}-\\frac{4{x}^{4}}{{x}^{6}}+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{6}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{{x}^{6}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}})}{(1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when $x$ is very large, the terms $\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}},$ $\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}$ and $\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}$ become very small. Therefore, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{({x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}})}{(1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}})} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{{x}^{2}-0+0}{1-0} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not a constant, which means that $y=f(x)$ does not have a horizontal asymptote." 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399789 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399790 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399791 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399792 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399793 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399788 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399788 1077 "selection" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399788 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399790 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399788 1080 #uuid "d0eba56c-3f43-5bc0-93ac-9b6c1e733e11" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399789 1081 "y=-1" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399789 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399789 1084 #uuid "ae1f564d-015d-531a-84ba-220e72e5068b" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399790 1081 "No horizontal asymptotes" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399790 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399790 1084 #uuid "5cefa02b-c23b-5120-bf50-f5e584021c12" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399791 1081 "y=0" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399791 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399791 1084 #uuid "64a8fd7a-b8ce-5f62-8477-ec3c16462673" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399792 1081 "y=-2" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399792 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399792 1084 #uuid "2a57eba1-1adb-5f47-ab81-1ede087ed451" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399793 1081 "y=1" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399793 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399793 1084 #uuid "f73c86ea-5390-5440-876a-85ab356720c8" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399794 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399795 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399794 1069 "q-113245" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399794 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399794 1071 "The equation ${x}^{2}-6x+34=0$ can be written in the form $(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399794 1072 #uuid "ed379096-4def-51e1-8cd6-e568b470e309" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399794 1074 "We first move the constant to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x+34 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x & =-34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x & =-34 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2} & =-34 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9 & =-34 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =-25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-3,\\,q=-25,$ and $p+q=-28.$\n\nFinally, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =-25 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-25} \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm 5\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =3\\pm 5\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=3+5\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=3-5\\,\\text{i}.$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399796 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399797 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399798 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399799 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399800 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399795 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399795 1077 "selection" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399795 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399796 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399795 1080 #uuid "abb7896d-c7f4-5b7b-a55d-ac98d8904d0e" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399796 1081 "p+q=-28,\\,x=3\\pm 5\\,\\text{i}" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399796 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399796 1084 #uuid "ac5d4b19-8c81-5ba1-996a-70b59878a1fa" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399797 1081 "p+q=22,\\,x=3\\pm 5\\,\\text{i}" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399797 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399797 1084 #uuid "6512548c-dca0-5e35-9fae-cb9552f71f4b" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399798 1081 "p+q=-28,\\,x=5\\pm 3\\,\\text{i}" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399798 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399798 1084 #uuid "ea660700-9472-591c-8a60-b82ac1eb0a78" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399799 1081 "p+q=22,\\,x=5\\pm 3\\,\\text{i}" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399799 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399799 1084 #uuid "aa2d981b-ddf0-5166-b28f-034d57bae937" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399800 1081 "p+q=-28,\\,x