ligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+36 \\\\  & x-6\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-4} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-36x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,36x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{36x-216}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,212\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4.$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399831 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399832 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399833 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399834 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399835 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1077 "selection" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399835 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1080 #uuid "aeb0dafe-c8dd-5892-9eb8-f305e87ca008" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399831 1081 "$6x+48\\,$ and $\\,48x-8$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399831 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399831 1084 #uuid "e6409232-2d31-593b-90bb-8a5813883aaa" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399832 1081 "$6x-24\\,$ and $\\,24x-4$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399832 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399832 1084 #uuid "8add39dc-99a4-5ff4-9055-09c5f3363d40" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399833 1081 "$6x+30\\,$ and $\\,30x-6$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399833 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399833 1084 #uuid "aa8cd1cd-1378-56d5-a7ab-7daa3b9b05fe" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399834 1081 "$6x-36\\,$ and $\\,48x-4$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399834 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399834 1084 #uuid "29edcf41-1ad2-52f3-ab8d-9b28e983225b" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399835 1081 "$6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399835 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399835 1084 #uuid "f2683559-249d-5d23-9f72-d0c8764dba6c" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399836 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399837 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399836 1069 "q-114399" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399836 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399836 1071 "![](images/8f/8f20b09e85ce71a1001e7c701ebfafa3e6ac6c8adb29e8dfd47f256f37a29f5f.png)\n\nThe function $h(x)$ is continuous and twice-differentiable for all $x$ in $(-4,1.5)$ The graph $y={h}^{″}(x)$ is shown above. At what value(s) of $x$ does $h(x)$ have a point of inflection?" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399836 1072 #uuid "959a29f9-94e3-5ec3-bf75-8100c4fac3c4" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399836 1074 "First, notice that since $h(x)$ is twice-differentiable, the tangent line to the graph exists for all real $x.$\n\nInflection points occur when a graph changes concavity. In order for the graph to change concavity, the value of the second derivative ${h}^{″}(x)$ must switch signs. So, we are looking for points where the graph of ${h}^{″}(x)$ crosses the $x$-axis.\n\nWe can see that the graph $y={h}^{″}(x)$ crosses the $x$-axis at $x=-1$ and $x=1.$ \n\nTherefore, $h(x)$ has points of inflection at $x=-1$ and $x=1.$" 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399838 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399839 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399840 13194139533479 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399841 13194139533479 1